{title: I Cannot Tell}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: 1}
I cannot [C]tell why [C7]he, whom angels [F]worship[**]; Should set his [C]love u[Am]pon the sons of [D]men[G]
Or why, as [C]Shepherd, [C7]he should seek the [F]wanderers[**]; To bring them [C]back, they [**]know not how or [**]when[E7]
But this I [Am]know, that [F]he was born of [C]Mary[E7]; When Bethl'em's [Am]manger [F]was his only [G]home[**]
And that he [C]lived at [F]Nazareth and [C]laboured[Am]; And so the [C]Saviour, Saviour [G]of the world, is [C]come[**].
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
I cannot [C]tell how [C7]silently he [F]suffered[**]; As with his [C]peace he [Am]graced this place of [D]tear[G]s
Or how his [C]heart u[C7]pon the cross was [F]broken[**]; The crown of [C]pain to [**]three and thirty [**]years[E7]
But this I [Am]know, he [F]heals the broken[C]hearted[E7]; And stays our [Am]sin and [F]calms our lurking [G]fear[**]
And lifts the [C]burden [F]from the heavy [C]laden[Am]; For still the [C]Saviour, Saviour [G]of the world is [C]here[**].
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
I cannot [C]tell how [C7]he will win the [F]nations[**]; How he will [C]claim his [Am]earthly heri[D]tage[G]
How satis[C]fy the [C7]needs and aspi[F]rations[**]; Of east and [C]west, of [**]sinner and of [**]sage[E7]
But this I [Am]know, all [F]flesh shall see his [C]glo[E7]ry; And he shall [Am]reap the [F]harvest he has [G]sown[**]
And some glad [C]day his [F]sun will shine in [C]splen[Am]dour; When he the [C]Saviour, Saviour [G]of the world, is [C]known[**].
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
I cannot [C]tell how [C7]all the lands shall [F]worship[**]; When at his [C]bidding [Am]every storm is [D]stilled[G]
Or who can [C]say how [C7]great the jubi[F]lation[**]; When every [C]heart with [**]love and joy is [**]fille[E7]d
But this I [Am]know, the [F]skies will thrill with [C]rap[E7]ture; And myriad [Am]myriad [F]human voices [G]sing[**]
And earth to [C]heav'n, and [F]heav'n to earth, will [C]an[Am]swer; ‘At last the [C]Saviour, Saviour [G]of the world, is [C]King![**]'
{end_of_verse}
